# Shell scripts and Docker build files run inside Linux containers and must
# stay LF regardless of core.autocrlf on the checkout machine. This is not
# hypothetical: core.autocrlf=true on a Windows checkout converted
# services/malware-scanner/start.sh to CRLF, which breaks its shebang line
# entirely - the container failed with "exec: ./start.sh: not found" (exit
# 127) until this was caught and fixed. Without this file, the same file
# reverts to CRLF the next time it's checked out on Windows, silently
# reintroducing the exact same deploy failure.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
